{
  "_comment": "The cast: every painted or drawn element the site shows, in one place. The build reads this file — it finds each element's `marker` in every page it renders, so the register of WHAT IS WHERE (dist/cast.json, docs/CAST.md) is derived from the pages that really carry it, never typed by hand — and it refuses to build if an entry is on no page at all, or if a painting in site/art/index.json belongs to no entry. site/check-cast.mjs then opens every page in a browser and proves each element is in the DOM, loaded and sized where it says it is. `visible`: immediate = sized and loaded as soon as the page is up; eventually = arrives by JS (a timer, the fog, a scroll) so only presence is checked; canvas = a canvas with a size. `phone`: shown | smaller | hidden (display:none under 700px, by design) | skipped (JS does not draw it under 700px).",
  "entries": [
    { "id": "riders", "title": "Quixote and Sancho, riding to the windmill", "art": ["sancho", "quixote"], "marker": "class=\"riders\"", "selector": ".glass .riders", "layer": "hero · horizon-life", "motion": "css ride (into the plain, in depth) + mesh warp", "visible": "immediate", "phone": "smaller" },
